---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy policy — Trivarone"
  description="What personal information trivarone.com.au collects, why, who else sees it, and how to have it corrected or deleted. Prepared in accordance with the Australian Privacy Principles."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="titleblock">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="standfirst">
        What this website collects, why, and what happens to it. Prepared in accordance
        with the Australian Privacy Principles.
      </p>
      <p class="articlemeta">
        Last updated <time datetime="2026-10-28">28 October 2026</time>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede">
          Trivarone is a sole trader business based in Brisbane, Australia, owned and
          operated by Pradeep Anandraj. ABN 65 502 768 472.
        </p>

        <h2>What is collected</h2>

        <p>
          If you use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>, I collect your name, email
          address, business name, how you would like me to reply, and what you write in
          the message.
        </p>

        <p>
          If you ask for an <a href="/check/">AI Search Snapshot</a>, I collect your
          practice name, website address, the service you offer, your suburb, your email
          address and how you would like to hear back. Your name and a note are optional.
        </p>

        <p>
          I collect a phone number only if you give me one, and I use it only to reply
          to your request.
        </p>

        <p>
          If you email or telephone directly, Trivarone holds whatever you choose to
          provide.
        </p>

        <p>
          Nothing on this website requires you to create an account, and no payment
          information is collected here.
        </p>

        <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>

        <p>
          Like most websites, this one records technical information when a page is
          requested: the pages viewed, the approximate location, the browser and device
          used, and the site you arrived from.
        </p>

        <p>
          Trivarone uses Microsoft Clarity to understand how visitors use the site.
          Clarity records page interactions, which can include mouse movement, scrolling
          and clicks, and produces anonymised session recordings and heatmaps. It masks
          form fields and does not capture what you type into them. Microsoft states that
          this information is not used to train its models.
        </p>

        <p>
          I also use Google Analytics. It uses cookies to count visits and show me which
          pages are read.
        </p>

        <h2>Why it is collected</h2>

        <p>
          To respond to your enquiry. To carry out work you have asked for. To understand
          which parts of the site are useful and which are not.
        </p>

        <p>
          Nothing collected here is used for advertising, and nothing is sold.
        </p>

        <h2>Who else sees it</h2>

        <p>
          These services run this website. Each is based in the United States, so your
          information goes there.
        </p>

        <ul class="plainlist">
          <li><strong>Formspree</strong> receives what you type into a form here, keeps a copy, and emails it to me.</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts this website and keeps server logs.</li>
          <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> counts visits and shows me which pages are read.</li>
          <li><strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> shows me how visitors move through the site.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          To do the work, I also use ordinary business software: email, a record of the
          people I am working with, AI tools that help me write and transcribe, and video
          calls on a service such as Zoom or Google Meet. Some of these providers store
          information outside Australia. If I want to record a call so it can be
          transcribed, I tell you before the call starts, and you can say no.
        </p>

        <p>
          I do not sell personal information. I share it only with the services
          described on this page.
        </p>

        <h2>How long it is kept</h2>

        <p>
          Enquiries are kept while the conversation is active, and for a reasonable period
          afterwards in case you get back in touch. Contact records are kept while the
          relationship continues. Clarity session data is retained for 90 days.
        </p>

        <h2>Access, correction and deletion</h2>

        <p>
          You may ask what Trivarone holds about you, ask for it to be corrected, or ask
          for it to be deleted. Email <a href="mailto:pradeep@trivarone.com.au">pradeep@trivarone.com.au</a> and you will
          have a reply within five working days.
        </p>

        <h2>Complaints</h2>

        <p>
          If you have a concern about how your information has been handled, email <a href="mailto:pradeep@trivarone.com.au">pradeep@trivarone.com.au</a> and it will be
          looked into properly. You can also raise privacy concerns with the Office of the
          Australian Information Commissioner at <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>

        <p>
          If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--navy">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>Any questions about this, just ask.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede">
          If anything here is unclear, or you would like to know exactly what is held
          about you, send an email and you will get a straight answer.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Start a conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
